    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Defect ID:</b> DEF-002</p>

<p>The system processes and records a payment even when an invalid CVV is entered during checkout. The expected behavior is that the payment should be rejected and the user should be prompted to enter a valid CVV.</p>

<h2><a name="Preconditions"></a>Preconditions</h2>

<ol>
	<li>User is logged into the retail application.</li>
	<li>A valid product has been added to the cart.</li>
	<li>User has proceeded to the checkout/payment page.</li>
	<li>A valid payment method is available for testing.</li>
</ol>


<h2><a name="StepstoReproduce"></a>Steps to Reproduce</h2>

<ol>
	<li>Navigate to the checkout page.</li>
	<li>Add a product to the cart and proceed to payment.</li>
	<li>Enter a valid cardholder name.</li>
	<li>Enter a valid card number.</li>
	<li>Enter a valid expiry date.</li>
	<li>Enter an invalid CVV.</li>
	<li>Click the <b>Pay</b> or <b>Submit Payment</b> button.</li>
	<li>Observe the payment response and order status.</li>
</ol>


<h2><a name="ExpectedResult"></a>Expected Result</h2>

<ol>
	<li>The payment should not be processed.</li>
	<li>An appropriate validation message should be displayed, such as "Invalid CVV" or "Please enter a valid CVV".</li>
	<li>The user should remain on the payment page.</li>
	<li>No order payment should be recorded.</li>
	<li>The order status should remain unpaid or pending payment.</li>
	<li>No payment confirmation or success message should be displayed.</li>
</ol>


<h2><a name="ActualResult"></a>Actual Result</h2>

<ol>
	<li>The payment was successfully processed.</li>
	<li>The order payment was recorded in the system.</li>
	<li>The order status changed to Paid.</li>
	<li>A payment confirmation message was displayed.</li>
</ol>


<h2><a name="Impact"></a>Impact</h2>

<p>Invalid payment information is accepted.</p>

<p>Financial transactions may be recorded incorrectly.</p>

<p>Payment validation business rules are bypassed.</p>

<p>Potential risk of fraudulent or failed payment processing.</p>


<p><b>Severity:</b> Critical</p>

<p><b>Priority:</b> High</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

