    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Defect ID:</b> DEF-001</p>

<p>The system accepts and stores a payment method with an expired card expiry date. The API returns a successful response (201 Created) instead of validating and rejecting the expired card.</p>

<p><b>Preconditions</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>User is authenticated.</li>
	<li>Payment Methods API is available.</li>
	<li>Postman is configured with the required authorization headers.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Steps to Reproduce</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>Open Postman.</li>
	<li>Send a POST request to <tt>/api/PaymentMethods</tt>.</li>
	<li>Use the following request body: {<br/>
  "cardholderName": "Test Customer One",<br/>
  "cardNumber": "1521485615648651",<br/>
  "brand": "Visa",<br/>
  "expiry": "01/01",<br/>
  "isDefault": true<br/>
}</li>
</ol>


<ol>
	<li>Click <b>Send</b>.</li>
	<li>Observe the response returned by the API.</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Expected Result</b></p>

<p>The system should validate the expiry date and reject the request with an appropriate error message  and a 400 Bad Request response.</p>

<p><b>Actual Result</b></p>

<p>The API accepts the expired card and returns a <b>201 Created</b> response. The payment method is successfully created and stored in the system.</p>

<h2><a name="Impact"></a>Impact</h2>

<ul>
	<li>Invalid payment methods can be stored in the system.</li>
	<li>Users may attempt transactions using expired cards.</li>
	<li>Violates payment validation business rules.</li>
	<li>Could lead to payment processing failures during checkout.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Severity:</b> High</p>

<p><b>Priority:</b> High</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

