<p><ins><b>FR-002: Order Management (Creation, Modification, Cancellation)</b></ins></p>

<p><b>SQL: Order data integrity queries</b></p>

<div class='table-wrap'>
<table class='confluenceTable'><tbody>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Test Case ID</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Objective</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Precondition</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Test Steps</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Expected Results</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Actual Results</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Status</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>T-DB-INT-001</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Check if the order total stored in the database matches the calculated total of the items in the order.</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'> <br/>
Orders and order item records exist in the database.</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'><ol>
	<li>Connect to the database.</li>
	<li>Run the SQL query on the Orders table.</li>
	<li>Retrieve OrderId, StoredTotal, and ItemCount values.</li>
	<li>Compare the stored order total with the calculated total from order items.</li>
	<li>Review the results.</li>
</ol>
</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>All orders should display <b>"Match"</b> and the stored total should be accurate for every order.</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>All orders returned <b>"Match"</b>. No mismatches were found between stored and calculated totals.</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Pass</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>T-DB-INT-002</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Verify that the Orders table does not contain duplicate Order IDs.</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'> <br/>
Database is accessible (<b>LewisStoresDb</b>). Orders table contains data.</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'><ol>
	<li>Connect to the database.</li>
	<li>Run the SQL query to identify duplicate Order IDs.</li>
	<li>Review the query results.</li>
	<li>Verify whether any records are returned.</li>
</ol>
</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'> <br/>
No records should be returned. If records are returned, duplicate Order IDs exist in the Orders table.</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'> <br/>
No records were returned by the query, indicating that no duplicate Order IDs exist in the Orders table.</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Pass</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>T-DB-INT-003</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'> <br/>
Ensure that when an order is cancelled, the inventory quantity is restored correctly.</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'> <br/>
Product exists in inventory.<br/>
Order has been placed successfully.</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'> 
<ol>
	<li>Create a new order for a product.</li>
	<li>Note the current stock quantity of the product.</li>
	<li>Cancel the created order.</li>
	<li>Check the inventory stock quantity again.</li>
	<li>Verify inventory status and stock levels.</li>
</ol>
</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>The cancelled order should be reversed.<br/>
The product stock quantity should increase back to its original value.<br/>
Inventory status should remain valid with no negative stock values.</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'> <br/>
After cancelling the order, the inventory quantity was successfully restored.<br/>
The stock level increased back to the correct available quantity.<br/>
Inventory status remained <b>VALID</b> with no negative stock values.<br/>
No data inconsistencies were observed in the Products table.</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Pass</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>T-DB-INT-004</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Confirm Order Status Transitions Are Valid</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Database <b>LewisStoresDb</b> is accessible.<br/>
Orders table contains existing records with multiple statuses.</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'> 
<ol>
	<li>Connect to the <b>LewisStoresDb</b> database.</li>
	<li>Execute the SQL query.</li>
	<li>Review grouped order status results.</li>
	<li>Validate that all statuses are correctly aggregated.</li>
	<li>Confirm percentage calculation is accurate.</li>
	<li>Ensure no invalid or null statuses exist.</li>
</ol>
</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>All order statuses are grouped correctly without duplication.<br/>
Each status reflects an accurate count of orders.<br/>
Percentage values correctly represent each status proportion of total orders.<br/>
No missing, null, or invalid status values exist in the dataset.<br/>
Status transitions are consistently represented in the database.</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'> <br/>
Query executed successfully on the Orders table.<br/>
System returned grouped order status distribution without errors.<br/>
All existing order statuses were successfully aggregated and displayed.<br/>
No invalid, duplicate grouping anomalies, or null status values were detected.<br/>
Percentage calculations were generated for each status based on total order count.</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>Pass</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>


