    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Title</b><br/>
Successful Settlement of Authorized Payment</p>

<p><b>Preconditions</b><br/>
1. An order has been successfully created via the Orders API.<br/>
2. A payment has been successfully authorized and has a status of Authorized.<br/>
3. The authorized payment is eligible for settlement according to business rules.<br/>
4. Valid authentication credentials/token are available.<br/>
5. The Payment Settlement API endpoint is available and accessible in Postman.<br/>
6. The Payment ID and Order ID are known and available for testing.</p>

<p><b>Test Steps</b><br/>
1. Open Postman.<br/>
2. Retrieve the payment details using the Payment API and verify the payment status is Authorized.<br/>
3. Send a POST request to the Payment Settlement endpoint .<br/>
4. Include the required authentication token and headers.<br/>
5. Submit the settlement request.<br/>
6. Verify that a successful response status code (200 OK or 201 Created) is returned.<br/>
7. Retrieve the payment details using the Payment API.<br/>
8. Retrieve the order details using the Orders API.<br/>
9. Verify the order status has been updated according to business rules.<br/>
10. Retrieve the transaction history for the payment or order.</p>

<p><b>Expected Results</b><br/>
1. The settlement request is processed successfully.<br/>
2. The API returns a successful response status code.<br/>
3. The settled amount matches the originally authorized payment amount.<br/>
4. The associated order status is updated according to business rules (Processing).<br/>
5. Settlement date, transaction reference, and audit information are recorded successfully.</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

