    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Title</b><br/>
Reject Payment with Invalid CVV</p>

<p><b>Preconditions</b><br/>
1. User is logged into the retail application.<br/>
2. A valid product has been added to the cart.<br/>
3. User has proceeded to the checkout/payment page.<br/>
4. A valid payment method is available for testing.</p>

<p><b>Test Steps</b><br/>
1. Navigate to the checkout page.<br/>
2. Add a product to the cart and proceed to payment.<br/>
3. Enter a valid cardholder name.<br/>
4. Enter a valid card number.<br/>
5. Enter a valid expiry date.<br/>
6. Enter an invalid CVV <br/>
7. Click the Pay or Submit Payment button.<br/>
8. Observe the payment response and order status.</p>

<p><b>Expected Results</b><br/>
1. The payment is not processed.<br/>
2. An appropriate validation message is displayed, such as "Invalid CVV" or "Please enter a valid CVV".<br/>
3. The user remains on the payment page.<br/>
4. No order payment is recorded.<br/>
5. The order status remains unpaid or pending payment.6. No confirmation or successful payment message is displayed.</p>

<p><b>Actual resuls</b><br/>
The payment was processed.<br/>
Order payment was recorded</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

