    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Title:</b> Reject Payment with Invalid Card Number Format</p>

<p><b>Preconditions:</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>Payment Authorization API endpoint is available and accessible.</li>
	<li>Valid API credentials or authentication token are configured in Postman.</li>
	<li>Merchant account is active and authorized to process payment transactions.</li>
	<li>Test environment is operational.</li>
	<li>An invalid card number format is available for testing</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Test Steps:</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>Open Postman and create/select the Payment Authorization API request.</li>
	<li>Configure the request method and endpoint URL.</li>
	<li>Add the required authentication headers.</li>
	<li>Populate the request body with payment details, using an invalid card number format while providing valid values for all other required fields (expiry date, CVV, cardholder name, and transaction amount).</li>
	<li>Send the request to the Payment Authorization API.</li>
	<li>Review the API response.</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Expected Result:</b><br/>
The Payment Authorization API rejects the request and returns an appropriate client error status code. The response contains a validation error message indicating that the card number format is invalid. No authorization or transaction ID is generated, the payment is not authorized, and no funds are reserved or captured.</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

