    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Title</b> <br/>
Prevent Duplicate Charge for Same Transaction</p>

<p><b>Preconditions</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>User is logged into the application.</li>
	<li>At least one item has been added to the shopping cart.</li>
	<li>User has navigated to the payment page.</li>
	<li>A valid payment method is available.</li>
	<li>The payment system supports duplicate transaction prevention</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Test steps</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>Enter valid payment details.</li>
	<li>Click the Pay Now button to submit the payment.</li>
	<li>Before receiving a response, attempt to submit the same payment again by clicking Pay Now multiple times or resending the same transaction request.</li>
	<li>Wait for the payment processing to complete.</li>
	<li>Review the payment and order records.</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Expected Results</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>The payment is processed successfully only once.</li>
	<li>Only one charge is created for the transaction.</li>
	<li>Duplicate payment requests are rejected, ignored, or identified as duplicates by the system.</li>
	<li>Only one order is created for the purchase.</li>
	<li>The user receives an appropriate message indicating that the transaction has already been processed, if applicable.</li>
	<li>No duplicate charges appear in the payment records.</li>
	<li>Transaction logs show that duplicate requests were handled correctly without creating additional charges.</li>
</ol>

            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

