    <table cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center">
    <tr>
        <td bgcolor="#bbbbbb" width="1%" nowrap align="center">
            &nbsp;<font color="#ffffff"><b>Description</b></font>&nbsp;
        </td>
        <td>&nbsp;</td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Title:</b> Successful Payment Authorization with Valid Card</p>

<h4><a name="Preconditions"></a>Preconditions</h4>

<p>1. User has access to the payment/checkout page.<br/>
2. A valid payment card (e.g., Visa, Mastercard) with sufficient funds is available.<br/>
3.  Payment gateway/service is operational and connected to the test environment.<br/>
4. User has at least one item in the shopping cart or an invoice/order ready for payment.<br/>
5. Network connection is stable. </p>

<p>Test Steps<br/>
1. Navigate to the payment page <br/>
2. Verify that the order details and payment amount are displayed correctly.<br/>
3. Select the card payment option<br/>
4. Enter a valid card number. <br/>
5. Enter a valid expiry date. <br/>
6. Enter any other required billing information. <br/>
7. Click the Pay, Submit, or Authorize Payment button. <br/>
8. Wait for the payment authorization response from the payment gateway.</p>

<p>Expected results <br/>
1. Checkout/payment page loads successfully. <br/>
2. Order details and total payment amount are accurate. <br/>
3. Card payment option is selectable. <br/>
4. Valid card and billing information are accepted without validation errors. <br/>
5. Payment request is submitted successfully. <br/>
6.  Payment is successfully authorized by the payment gateway. A success message is displayed to the user, an authorization code/transaction ID is generated, and the order status is updated appropriately. No error message are displayed.</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

