    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Title</b><br/>
Verifying Inventory Restores After Return Receipt</p>

<p><b>Preconditions</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>A product exists in the inventory with a known stock quantity.</li>
	<li>An order containing the product has been successfully completed and delivered.</li>
	<li>The customer has initiated a return for the product.</li>
	<li>The returned item has been physically received and is eligible to be restocked.</li>
	<li>Access to inventory records is available for verification.</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Test steps</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>Verify the current inventory quantity of the product.</li>
	<li>Navigate to the return management section.</li>
	<li>Locate the return request for the product.</li>
	<li>Mark the returned item as received.</li>
	<li>Complete the return receipt process.</li>
	<li>Check the updated inventory quantity for the product.</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Expected Results</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>The return receipt is processed successfully.</li>
	<li>The return status is updated to indicate the item has been received.</li>
	<li>The inventory quantity is increased by the quantity of the returned item.</li>
	<li>The updated inventory reflects the returned stock accurately.</li>
	<li>No duplicate inventory adjustments occur.</li>
	<li>Inventory records remain consistent and accurate after the return receipt process.</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Actual result</b><br/>
Inventory never changed in database when Order was placed - Inventory stayed the same.<br/>
Returns get affected as Phantom stock now exists within the database. </p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

