    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Title</b> <br/>
Verify Inventory Decrements Correctly After Order Placement </p>

<p><b>Preconditions</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>A product exists in the database with a known inventory quantity.</li>
	<li>User is logged into the application.</li>
	<li>The product is available for purchase.</li>
	<li>Access to the database is available for verification.</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Test steps</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>Execute an SQL query to retrieve the current inventory quantity of the product (SELECT ProductID, ProductName, QuantityOnHand<br/>
FROM Products<br/>
WHERE ProductID = 103<img class="emoticon" src="/images/icons/emoticons/wink.png" height="16" width="16" align="absmiddle" alt="" border="0"/></li>
	<li>Place an order for a specific quantity of the product</li>
	<li>Complete the order successfully.</li>
	<li>Execute the SQL query again to retrieve the updated inventory quantity.</li>
	<li>Compare the inventory quantity before and after the order placement.</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Expected Results</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>The order is created successfully.</li>
	<li>The inventory quantity in the database is reduced by the ordered amount..</li>
	<li>No negative inventory values are recorded.</li>
	<li>The inventory record reflects the correct remaining stock quantity.</li>
</ol>

            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

