    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Test objective</b></p>

<p>Confirm that every Deliveries record with Status = 'Delivered' carries both a DeliveredAtUtc timestamp and a CurrentLocation value confirming receipt. Missing POD evidence is a compliance and customer dispute risk.</p>

<p><b>SQL validation approach</b></p>

<p>INNER JOIN Deliveries → Orders, filter Status = 'Delivered', assert DeliveredAtUtc IS NOT NULL and CurrentLocation LIKE '%Delivered%'. ViolationReason column distinguishes missing timestamp from missing location confirmation.</p>

<p><b>Expected result</b></p>

<p>0 rows returned — all delivered orders have complete POD evidence.</p>

<p><b>Actual result</b></p>

<p>0 rows returned. ORD-003 (the sole Delivered record) has DeliveredAtUtc set and CurrentLocation = 'Delivered to recipient'.</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

