    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Test objective</b></p>

<p>Confirm that timestamp evidence matches the declared delivery status. A record marked Shipped or Delivered must have ShippedAtUtc populated; a Delivered record must also have DeliveredAtUtc, and it must not precede ShippedAtUtc.</p>

<p><b>SQL validation approach</b></p>

<p>Four WHERE conditions check: Shipped with null ShippedAtUtc, Delivered with null ShippedAtUtc, Delivered with null DeliveredAtUtc, and DeliveredAtUtc earlier than ShippedAtUtc. ViolationReason column identifies the specific breach.</p>

<p><b>Expected result</b></p>

<p>0 rows returned — all status transitions are timestamp-consistent.</p>

<p><b>Actual result</b></p>

<p>0 rows returned. ORD-002 (Shipped) and ORD-003 (Delivered) both carry valid ShippedAtUtc and DeliveredAtUtc values in correct chronological order.</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

