    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Test Case: Validate Cancelled Order Returns Inventory Quantity</b></p>

<p><b>Objective:</b><br/>
Ensure that when an order is cancelled, the inventory quantity is restored correctly.</p>

<p><b>Preconditions:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>Product exists in inventory</li>
	<li>Order has been placed successfully</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Test Steps:</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>Create a new order for a product.</li>
	<li>Note the current stock quantity of the product.</li>
	<li>Cancel the created order.</li>
	<li>Check the inventory stock quantity again.</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Expected Result:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>The cancelled order should be reversed.</li>
	<li>The product stock quantity should increase back to its original value.</li>
	<li>Inventory status should remain valid (no negative stock).</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Actual Result:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>After cancelling the order, the inventory quantity was successfully restored.</li>
	<li>The stock level increased back to the correct available quantity.</li>
	<li>Inventory status remained <b>VALID</b> with no negative stock values.</li>
	<li>No data inconsistencies were observed in the Products table.</li>
</ul>


<p><span class="image-wrap" style=""><img src="https://redacademy-team-quallityengineer.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/10462" alt="image-20260521-081806.png" width="395" style="border: 0px solid black" /></span></p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

