    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <h3><a name="TestCase%3AConfirmNoDuplicateOrderIDsExist"></a><b>Test Case: Confirm No Duplicate Order IDs Exist</b></h3>

<p><b>Description:</b><br/>
Verify that the Orders table does not contain duplicate Order IDs.</p>

<p><b>Preconditions:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>Database is accessible (<tt>LewisStoresDb</tt>)</li>
	<li>Orders table contains data</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Test Steps:</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>Run the following SQL query:
<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre>SELECT 
    Id AS OrderId,
    COUNT(*) AS DuplicateCount
FROM Orders
GROUP BY Id
HAVING COUNT(*) &gt; 1;</pre>
</div></div></li>
	<li>Review the query results.</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Expected Result:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>No records should be returned.</li>
	<li>If results are returned, it indicates duplicate Order IDs exist in the Orders table.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Actual Result:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>No records should be returned.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Status:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>Pass</li>
</ul>


<p><span class="image-wrap" style=""><img src="https://redacademy-team-quallityengineer.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/10461" alt="image-20260521-081351.png" width="380" style="border: 0px solid black" /></span></p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

